\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] CNmodRELSENT1
\item[* relevant examples:] 
hombre + [x2 el ve ] $\rightarrow$ [hombre [??a que el ve ],]\\
\item[* language:] Spanish
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CNformation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) modrules
\item[* date of creation:] 11-OCT-1988 11:57:36  
\item[* author:] Franciska de Jong
\item[* copied from:] --
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 01/11/88\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette appelo
\item date: 20/04/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Changed superdeixis conditions/actions for independent sentences. Allowed are:
- presentdeixis without refvar and CN.superdeixis <> presentdeixis\\
- presentdeixis with refvar
- pastdeixis without refvar and CN.superdeixis <> pastdeixis\\
- pastdeixis with refvar
\item date: 31/09/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster\\
attribute "contraction" for PREP introduced; the reason is that not only 'a' or 
'de' should glue with 'el', but also "idiom prepositions" ending on 'a' or 'de'.
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] Modification of a CN by a restrictive, finite, relative SENTENCE.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
The subrules can be divided in the following way:\\
subrule 1 and 2 are for the relative pronoun {\em dat}\\
subrule 3 and 4 are for the relative pronoun {\em die}\\

In the first and third rule a comma is present behind the relative clause
both in generation and in analysis.\\
In the second and fourth subrule cases where no comma is present are dealt with
, only analytically.

\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] In analysis the absence 
of a comma behind the  relative sentence \'{i}s accepted, but in generation
a comma is always generated. 
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:] 
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
\item modifications: Dutch copy from this rule with superdeixis conditions/
actions. Adapted to supertiempo. Added some subrules from Dutch extra that 
seemed necessary to me.\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}



\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
 RULE RCNmodanterel1          (* assignEform not yet accounted for *)
                       (* Is dit nodig in het Spaans ? EA *)
< SUBST:
  m1:CN{CNrec1}[I1:mu1] 
  m2:I2::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
                 [ subjrel/CNVAR{CNVARrec1},
                   mu2,
                   predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                         [ mu3,
                           head/I3::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4] 
                         ] 
                 ]
>

< m :CN{CNrec1}
       [ relsentrel/I2::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec2}
               [ mu2,
                 predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                        [ mu3,
                          head/I3::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu4] 
                        ] 
               ],
         I1:mu1 
       ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: NOT EXIST (mu1, [head/EN{ENrec1}])
       I2: SENTENCErec2 = 
               { mood       : anterelative
                 PROsubject : true
                 modus      : prespart                 
               }
       I3: (VERBrec1.status = bareV) OR
           (VERBrec1.status = partV)
      >

   PARAMETERS
      <
       LEVEL
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: (CNVARrec1.index = LEVEL) AND
              (CNVARrec1 =  COPYT_CNtoVAR(CNrec1) EXCEPT FOR [cases] ) AND
              (CNVARrec1.cases = [Nominative])
              (* req and env still to be accounted for *)

              C11: (* temporally independent *)
                   (SENTENCErec1.supertiempo = omegatiempo) AND
                   (((SENTENCErec1.tiempo = presente) AND
                     (((QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu2)) AND
                       (CNrec1.supertiempo <> presente)
                      ) OR
                      (NOT QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu2))
                      )
                     )
                    ) OR
                    ((SENTENCErec1.tiempo = pasado) AND
                     (((QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu2)) AND
                       (CNrec1.supertiempo <> pasado)
                      ) OR
                      (NOT QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu2))
                      )
                     )
                    )
                   )
              A11: SENTENCErec2 := SENTENCErec1;

              C12: (* temporally dependent *)
                   (CNrec1.supertiempo = SENTENCErec1.supertiempo) AND
                   (SENTENCErec1.tiempo = omegatiempo)
              A12: SENTENCErec2 := SENTENCErec1;
                   SENTENCErec2.supertiempo := omegatiempo;
           A1: @
         >


      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
              C11: (* temporally independent *)
                   SENTENCErec2.supertiempo = omegatiempo AND
                   NOT (QUOTE_temprefnotfound(mu2))
              A11: SENTENCErec1 := SENTENCErec2;

              C12: (* temporally dependent *)
                   SENTENCErec2.supertiempo = omegatiempo AND
                   SENTENCErec2.tiempo = omegatiempo
              A12: SENTENCErec1:= SENTENCErec2;
                   SENTENCErec1.supertiempo := CNrec1.supertiempo;

          A1: CNVARrec1.index := LEVEL;
              CNVARrec1 := COPYT_CNtoVAR(CNrec1);
              CNVARrec1.cases := [Nominative];
                            (* req and env still to be accounted for *)

         >

&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] CNmodanterel1
\item[* relevant examples:]
kind + [x1 lopend ] $\rightarrow$ [lopend kind]\\
man  + [x1 z'n kinderen hatend] $\rightarrow$ [z'n kinderen hatend man]
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) Dutch
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] NP-subgrammar
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) Modrules
\item[* date of creation:] 11-MAR-1987 15:27:48  
\item[* author:] Elly van Munster, Jan Odijk
\item[* copied from:]--
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 22/MAR/1988\ \ \ \ \ author: Franciska de Jong
\item date: 01/11/88\ \ \ \ \ author: LIsette Appelo
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To modify a CN by an anterelative sentence containing
a present participle.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
The e-form of the participle has not been accounted for in this rule, in
accordance with the treatment of the e-form for adjectives.
Perhaps, however, this must be done in this rule.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
The participle must crucially be the last element in the SENTENCE for
its functioning as an anterelsent to be possible. Hence there are no
variables behind the verb.
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:] dna
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] none
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:] 
